Contact pressure, compliance and the loaded interface (@mech-contact: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mechanical-engineering, #source "../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W", #mechanical-engineering "../measurement/Strain-gauges-full-field-measurements-and-model-validation.lingua#r_5GX4N1Q7XDQ9DPVWVJWSGR9N36", #clean-manufacturing "../../../production/clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control/surfaces/Contact-models-share-conventions-before-they-share-numbers.lingua#r_425C0AZ76A3BN6W8MEPGVY0D15") { r_14H9DG80V3YYNWP3MP73TC1VMT
**Read:** [Applied Mechanics of Solids — Allan F. Bower](../sources/Applied-Mechanics-of-Solids-Bower.lingua#r_109WFZBWMEMGHV9TGFD22H2F1W), section 5.4 and section 8.8; connect the existing friction account to elastic deformation of the contacting bodies.

Two nominally rigid curved surfaces touch over a small region because the materials deform. In the ideal Hertz sphere-on-half-space model, effective modulus satisfies 1/E* = (1−ν₁²)/E₁ + (1−ν₂²)/E₂ and contact radius a = (3FR*/(4E*))^(1/3), with the geometry convention stated. Peak pressure is 3F/(2πa²). The model assumes smooth elastic bodies, small contact relative to curvature and dimensions, and appropriate nonadhesive frictionless contact.

For F = 100 N, R* = 10 mm and E* = 100 GPa, a is about 0.196 mm and peak pressure about 1.24 GPa. A small total force can produce a large local stress. Check elastic validity instead of assuming the calculated pressure is physically sustainable.

Roughness, coatings, lubrication, plasticity, adhesion and tangential traction change the interface problem. Surface pressure and subsurface shear matter differently for indentation, fretting, rolling-contact fatigue and wear. A contact stiffness can also change alignment and natural frequencies.

**Work:** Derive the Hertz scaling and compare its prediction with a planar nominal-pressure estimate. Identify the relevant failure or compliance question for a bearing, gear tooth or clamp. For a finite-element contact model, check separation, penetration, friction law, discretization and equilibrium rather than interpreting a coloured pressure contour alone.

